.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/postcss-value-parser Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "postcss-value-parser"
.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
Transforms CSS declaration values and at-rule parameters into a tree of nodes, and provides a simple traversal API\&.
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
var valueParser = require('postcss\-value\-parser');
var cssBackgroundValue = 'url(foo\&.png) no\-repeat 40px 73%';
var parsedValue = valueParser(cssBackgroundValue);
// parsedValue exposes an API described below,
// e\&.g\&. parsedValue\&.walk(\&.\&.), parsedValue\&.toString(), etc\&.
.fi
.PP

.PP
For example, parsing the value \fRrgba(233, 45, 66, \&.5)\fP will return the following:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  nodes: [
    {
      type: 'function',
      value: 'rgba',
      before: '',
      after: '',
      nodes: [
        { type: 'word', value: '233' },
        { type: 'div', value: ',', before: '', after: ' ' },
        { type: 'word', value: '45' },
        { type: 'div', value: ',', before: '', after: ' ' },
        { type: 'word', value: '66' },
        { type: 'div', value: ',', before: ' ', after: '' },
        { type: 'word', value: '\&.5' }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
If you wanted to convert each \fRrgba()\fP value in \fRsourceCSS\fP to a hex value, you could do so like this:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var valueParser = require('postcss\-value\-parser');

var parsed = valueParser(sourceCSS);

// walk() will visit all the of the nodes in the tree,
// invoking the callback for each\&.
parsed\&.walk(function (node) {

  // Since we only want to transform rgba() values,
  // we can ignore anything else\&.
  if (node\&.type !== 'function' && node\&.value !== 'rgba') return;

  // We can make an array of the rgba() arguments to feed to a
  // convertToHex() function
  var color = node\&.nodes\&.filter(function (node) {
    return node\&.type === 'word';
  })\&.map(function (node) {
    return Number(node\&.value);
  }); // [233, 45, 66, \&.5]

  // Now we will transform the existing rgba() function node
  // into a word node with the hex value
  node\&.type = 'word';
  node\&.value = convertToHex(color);
})

parsed\&.toString(); // #E92D42
.fi
.PP
.SH "Nodes"
.PP
Each node is an object with these common properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBtype\fP: The type of node (\fRword\fP, \fRstring\fP, \fRdiv\fP, \fRspace\fP, \fRcomment\fP, or \fRfunction\fP)\&. Each type is documented below\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBvalue\fP: Each node has a \fRvalue\fP property; but what exactly \fRvalue\fP means is specific to the node type\&. Details are documented for each type below\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBsourceIndex\fP: The starting index of the node within the original source string\&. For example, given the source string \fR10px 20px\fP, the \fRword\fP node whose value is \fR20px\fP will have a \fRsourceIndex\fP of \fR5\fP\&.
.PP
.SS "word"
The catch-all node type that includes keywords (e\&.g\&. \fRno-repeat\fP), quantities (e\&.g\&. \fR20px\fP, \fR75%\fP, \fR1\&.5\fP), and hex colors (e\&.g\&. \fR#e6e6e6\fP)\&.

.PP
Node-specific properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBvalue\fP: The "word" itself\&.
.PP
.SS "string"
A quoted string value, e\&.g\&. \fR"something"\fP in \fRcontent: "something";\fP\&.

.PP
Node-specific properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBvalue\fP: The text content of the string\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBquote\fP: The quotation mark surrounding the string, either \fR"\fP or \fR'\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBunclosed\fP: \fRtrue\fP if the string was not closed properly\&. e\&.g\&. \fR"unclosed string \fP\&.
.PP
.SS "div"
A divider, for example

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR,\fP in \fRanimation-duration: 1s, 2s, 3s\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR/\fP in \fRborder-radius: 10px / 23px\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR:\fP in \fR(min-width: 700px)\fP
.PP

.PP
Node-specific properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBvalue\fP: The divider character\&. Either \fR,\fP, \fR/\fP, or \fR:\fP (see examples above)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBbefore\fP: Whitespace before the divider\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBafter\fP: Whitespace after the divider\&.
.PP
.SS "space"
Whitespace used as a separator, e\&.g\&. \fR \fP occurring twice in \fRborder: 1px solid black;\fP\&.

.PP
Node-specific properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBvalue\fP: The whitespace itself\&.
.PP
.SS "comment"
A CSS comment starts with \fR/*\fP and ends with \fR*/\fP

.PP
Node-specific properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBvalue\fP: The comment value without \fR/*\fP and \fR*/\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBunclosed\fP: \fRtrue\fP if the comment was not closed properly\&. e\&.g\&. \fR/* comment without an end \fP\&.
.PP
.SS "function"
A CSS function, e\&.g\&. \fRrgb(0,0,0)\fP or \fRurl(foo\&.bar)\fP\&.

.PP
Function nodes have nodes nested within them: the function arguments\&.

.PP
Additional properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBvalue\fP: The name of the function, e\&.g\&. \fRrgb\fP in \fRrgb(0,0,0)\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBbefore\fP: Whitespace after the opening parenthesis and before the first argument, e\&.g\&. \fR \fP in \fRrgb(  0,0,0)\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBafter\fP: Whitespace before the closing parenthesis and after the last argument, e\&.g\&. \fR \fP in \fRrgb(0,0,0  )\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBnodes\fP: More nodes representing the arguments to the function\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBunclosed\fP: \fRtrue\fP if the parentheses was not closed properly\&. e\&.g\&. \fR( unclosed-function \fP\&.
.PP

.PP
Media features surrounded by parentheses are considered functions with an empty value\&. For example, \fR(min-width: 700px)\fP parses to these nodes:

.PP
.PP
.nf
[
  {
    type: 'function', value: '', before: '', after: '',
    nodes: [
      { type: 'word', value: 'min\-width' },
      { type: 'div', value: ':', before: '', after: ' ' },
      { type: 'word', value: '700px' }
    ]
  }
]
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fRurl()\fP functions can be parsed a little bit differently depending on whether the first character in the argument is a quotation mark\&.

.PP
\fRurl( /gfx/img/bg\&.jpg )\fP parses to:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{ type: 'function', sourceIndex: 0, value: 'url', before: ' ', after: ' ', nodes: [
    { type: 'word', sourceIndex: 5, value: '/gfx/img/bg\&.jpg' }
] }
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fRurl( "/gfx/img/bg\&.jpg" )\fP, on the other hand, parses to:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{ type: 'function', sourceIndex: 0, value: 'url', before: ' ', after: ' ', nodes: [
     type: 'string', sourceIndex: 5, quote: '"', value: '/gfx/img/bg\&.jpg' },
] }
.fi
.PP
.SS "unicode-range"
The unicode-range CSS descriptor sets the specific range of characters to be used from a font defined by @font-face and made available for use on the current page (\fRunicode-range: U+0025-00FF\fP)\&.

.PP
Node-specific properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBvalue\fP: The "unicode-range" itself\&.
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.PP
.nf
var valueParser = require('postcss\-value\-parser');
.fi
.PP
.SS "valueParser\&.unit(quantity)"
Parses \fRquantity\fP, distinguishing the number from the unit\&. Returns an object like the following:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Given 2rem
{
  number: '2',
  unit: 'rem'
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
If the \fRquantity\fP argument cannot be parsed as a number, returns \fRfalse\fP\&.

.PP
\fIThis function does not parse complete values\fP: you cannot pass it \fR1px solid black\fP and expect \fRpx\fP as the unit\&. Instead, you should pass it single quantities only\&. Parse \fR1px solid black\fP, then pass it the stringified \fR1px\fP node (a \fRword\fP node) to parse the number and unit\&.
.SS "valueParser\&.stringify(nodes[, custom])"
Stringifies a node or array of nodes\&.

.PP
The \fRcustom\fP function is called for each \fRnode\fP; return a string to override the default behaviour\&.
.SS "valueParser\&.walk(nodes, callback[, bubble])"
Walks each provided node, recursively walking all descendent nodes within functions\&.

.PP
Returning \fRfalse\fP in the \fRcallback\fP will prevent traversal of descendent nodes (within functions)\&. You can use this feature to for shallow iteration, walking over only the \fIimmediate\fP children\&. \fINote: This only applies if \fRbubble\fP is \fRfalse\fP (which is the default)\&.\fP

.PP
By default, the tree is walked from the outermost node inwards\&. To reverse the direction, pass \fRtrue\fP for the \fRbubble\fP argument\&.

.PP
The \fRcallback\fP is invoked with three arguments: \fRcallback(node, index, nodes)\fP\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnode\fP: The current node\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRindex\fP: The index of the current node\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnodes\fP: The complete nodes array passed to \fRwalk()\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
Returns the \fRvalueParser\fP instance\&.
.SS "var parsed = valueParser(value)"
Returns the parsed node tree\&.
.SS "parsed\&.nodes"
The array of nodes\&.
.SS "parsed\&.toString()"
Stringifies the node tree\&.
.SS "parsed\&.walk(callback[, bubble])"
Walks each node inside \fRparsed\&.nodes\fP\&. See the documentation for \fRvalueParser\&.walk()\fP above\&.
